Prompts: Role Assignment

Purpose:
  Map functional roles to tech stack and layers based on prompt input.
  Enables human approval of proposed role assignments.

Owns: ./

ReadOrder:
   1 @INDEX.sdd
   2 @role-mapper.sdd
   3 @provisioning-trigger.sdd
   4 @human-approval.sdd

Roles:
  BACKEND:
    Languages: go, python, java, csharp, rust, nodejs
    Frameworks: gin, echo, spring, django, fastapi, express, nestjs
    Databases: postgresql, mysql, mongodb, redis

  FRONTEND:
    Languages: javascript, typescript
    Frameworks: react, vue, angular, svelte, nextjs
    Databases: (none)

  MOBILE:
    Languages: dart, swift, kotlin
    Frameworks: flutter, react-native, swiftui, compose
    Databases: (none)

  DATABASE:
    Databases: postgresql, mysql, mongodb, redis, elasticsearch, cassandra

  QA:
    Tools: jest, pytest, selenium, cypress, playwright, jmeter
    Frameworks: (testing frameworks)

  DEVOPS:
    Platforms: docker, kubernetes, aws, azure, gcp, terraform
    Tools: jenkins, github-actions, gitlab-ci, ansible

  SECURITY:
    Topics: authentication, authorization, encryption, owasp

  ARCHITECT:
    Topics: system-design, microservices, monolith, serverless

Rules:
  [RA1] Every tech stack element MUST map to exactly one role.
  [RA2] Role assignments MUST be proposed to human for approval.
  [RA3] Provisioning triggers MUST require human approval.
  [RA4] Role changes MUST be recorded in decisions/.

State: +
